  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the woman as the recipient of undeserved benefits",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the woman (person) in the meme, who is depicted as the recipient of social benefits. The user identifies with or imagines themselves as the one who is morally outraged by this perceived undeservingness, as implied by the top text 'how can this be allowed a free home and benefits?'. The projection is onto the visual entity 'woman' which is used to represent the stereotype of a woman receiving government assistance, and the user is implicitly positioned as the moral arbiter or critic of this situation.",
